WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.133
-Welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.868
You're here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:06.834
Thank you for watching.

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:08.801
Let's get to some news here.

00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:10.434
Well, guys, everybody is still
talking about Elon Musk

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:14.667
buying Twitter for $44 billion.

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:16.901
Yep.
First Tesla and now Twitter.

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:18.400
It's amazing how much
money you can save

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.767
when you don't have to pay
for gas, isn't it?

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:27.634
$44 billion. Not too shabby.

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:29.234
$44 billion. That's a lot.

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:31.667
That's almost three
printer cartridges from Staples.

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:33.300
You know, if you think about it.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.033
Seriously, you know you're rich
when you buy something for

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:40.367
$44 billion
and you're still rich.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.000
Yep, Musk says
he's going to bring back

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.767
free speech to Twitter.

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:48.167
It's a big deal,
because if it's true,

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:50.567
it means we'll finally be able
to talk about Bruno.

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:51.934
And...

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:56.100
Finally, it'll...

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:00.767
Yeah, Musk has
a lot of ideas for the app.

00:01:00.767 --> 00:01:04.234
He plans to defend free speech,
get rid of spam bots,

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:06.667
and make Jeff Bezos' head
the new Twitter egg.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.567
[ Pop! ]

00:01:13.033 --> 00:01:14.634
Of course, some people are
worried that Musk

00:01:14.634 --> 00:01:17.734
will have a
negative impact on Twitter.

00:01:17.734 --> 00:01:22.100
Yes, compared to the absolute
paradise it's been all along.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.501
Well, some news from Washington.

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:25.901
Today, it was announced that
Vice President Kamala Harris

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:28.434
has tested positive
for COVID-19.

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:32.133
Yeah. President Biden told
her to take her time recovering.

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:33.767
He was like, "When I was VP,

00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:36.334
I was gone for two years,
and nobody even noticed."

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.968
I don't know if she can do that.

00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:46.467
Thankfully,
Harris is feeling good

00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:47.701
and will remain isolated,

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:50.701
just like she has
since taking office.

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:53.868
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:55.734
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, boy.

00:01:55.734 --> 00:01:57.334
-Yeah, The White House
said that Harris

00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:59.901
has been nowhere near Biden
for over a week,

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:01.767
which pretty much tells you
all you need to know

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:02.868
about that relationship.

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:04.200
You're like...

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.868
Meanwhile, House Speaker
Nancy Pelosi

00:02:05.868 --> 00:02:09.334
just returned to work after
testing positive for COVID.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:10.901
And she said that
she spent her quarantine

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:13.634
watching all of "Bridgerton."

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:16.067
Which explains why
she was still feverish

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:17.467
three days after recovering.

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:20.901
♪♪

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:22.167
Wow!

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:25.634
Apparently,
Pelosi got really into it.

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:28.400
She was like, "Anthony can storm
my Capitol anytime."

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.234
And you go, "Whoa, hey!"

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:32.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:34.667
Listen to this.

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:36.767
A judge in New York is holding
former president Trump

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:40.968
in contempt of court for failing
to turn over documents,

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:44.501
and he's being fined $10,000
a day until he does.

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:47.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
Wow.

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:52.300
Trump's actually trying to
locate the documents right now.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.200
He's going through
his filing system of

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.501
buried, shredded, or flushed.

00:02:57.734 --> 00:03:00.567
[ As Trump ]
I think I buried that one.

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:03.534
I tried flushing, that didn't
work, so I buried it."

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:05.701
Hey, this is fun.

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:08.501
Today, Auntie Anne's gave away
free pretzels for

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:10.334
National Pretzel Day.

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:12.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.601
And if you celebrated, I'm sorry
you were stuck at the airport.

00:03:16.667 --> 00:03:17.734
Hey, get this.

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:21.234
A family in Massachusetts
won $5 million

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.200
from a lawsuit against
a country club

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:26.567
after their property was hit
with over 600 golf balls.

00:03:26.567 --> 00:03:28.934
The family was like,
"You know, when we moved

00:03:28.934 --> 00:03:30.300
directly next to a golf course,

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.834
we had no idea
this could happen."

00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:37.133
Every day for four years,
their Ring doorbell was like,

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:38.801
"Motion detected,
motion detected,

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:41.834
mo-mo-mo-mo-motion detected."

00:03:42.534 --> 00:03:43.734
Honestly, this is what happens

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:45.000
when you live
in a tiny windmill.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.701
Do you know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:50.100
Thank you.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:59.767
And, finally, it is Tuesday.
It is time for "WeTweet."

00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:00.834
Here we go, everybody.

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:05.100
-♪ "WeTweet" ♪

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:08.367
♪ "WeTweet" ♪

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:10.033
-Welcome to "WeTweet."

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:11.834
This is where we, as a group,

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:15.667
decide something that we
should post on Twitter, okay?

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:17.400
I'm going to show
you five different tweets,

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.501
and we're all going to vote on

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:20.467
whether you
like each one or not.

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.267
You all have voting clickers
at your seats.

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:23.634
Did you get them there?

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:26.467
I can just tell by the confusion
that, yes, it is working.

00:04:26.467 --> 00:04:29.234
Now, you can all vote for --

00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:30.434
Why is everyone
looking left and right?

00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:31.534
You have them now, right?

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:33.434
Okay?

00:04:33.434 --> 00:04:35.267
Wow. Okay, here we go.

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:37.968
You can all vote for...

00:04:37.968 --> 00:04:40.267
People are still
going like this.

00:04:40.267 --> 00:04:42.334
Either you have it or you don't.
Okay, here we go.

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:43.801
You can vote for
all of them, okay?

00:04:43.801 --> 00:04:45.067
That's the fun of the game.

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:46.901
You can vote for all of them,
whatever you want,

00:04:46.901 --> 00:04:48.534
and we'll see the results live.

00:04:48.534 --> 00:04:50.467
Or you can vote for
none of them,

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:51.767
if you don't feel like
doing this.

00:04:51.767 --> 00:04:54.067
You can just go,
"Jimmy, you do the work.

00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:56.300
I'm not doing the work for you.
Yeah."

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.734
Roots, you have clickers,
as well.

00:04:57.734 --> 00:04:58.868
-Yep.
-Yes, we do.

00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:01.167
-How correct have you been,
Tariq, on these?

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.133
-Oh, I'm always spot on.

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:05.234
-You know which one
is going to be tweeted.

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:06.801
-Absolutely. Yeah.

00:05:06.801 --> 00:05:08.567
-Quest?
-I'm 50/50.

00:05:08.567 --> 00:05:09.934
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:09.934 --> 00:05:11.801
-I know which ones they are,
but we didn't rehearse it,

00:05:11.801 --> 00:05:13.300
so The Roots do not know.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.767
And I think I know
which one it is, too,

00:05:14.767 --> 00:05:16.167
but I've been pretty good.

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:17.267
I think I've nailed it.

00:05:17.267 --> 00:05:20.000
-Uh, not so much.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.467
-You have no idea which one --

00:05:21.467 --> 00:05:23.334
what I'm voting for
or what I'm doing or --

00:05:23.334 --> 00:05:24.767
It's all -- It's private.

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:27.534
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:29.968
-Alright, whatever tweet
gets the most likes,

00:05:29.968 --> 00:05:31.734
we will tweet it out
live on the show,

00:05:31.734 --> 00:05:36.000
and you can all like it
and "WeTweet" it from home.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.267
Thank you.
It's a shared experience.

00:05:38.267 --> 00:05:40.434
You guys -- Are you guys ready
to have some fun?

00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:42.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
Alright, here we go.

00:05:42.934 --> 00:05:45.834
The first tweet is...

00:05:51.701 --> 00:05:54.834
Alright. Alright. Wow.
♪♪

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:59.100
Uh...I like that,

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:03.501
but I feel like the audience is,
like, tepid on that one.

00:06:03.501 --> 00:06:06.367
The votes are in.
Let's see the results.

00:06:06.367 --> 00:06:08.567
Alright, there you go.

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:11.567
It was, yeah, like almost 50/50,
but, yeah, it was a non-tweet.

00:06:11.567 --> 00:06:12.701
Here we go.
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:06:12.701 --> 00:06:15.501
Thank you, Damon.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:17.501
Alright, here's the next one.
The next one is...

00:06:22.868 --> 00:06:24.634
♪♪

00:06:24.634 --> 00:06:26.734
"You don't think
I can handle that?

00:06:28.067 --> 00:06:31.300
You don't think I can handle a
little bump and grind?"

00:06:35.634 --> 00:06:37.701
Let's see --
Let's see the results.

00:06:37.701 --> 00:06:38.701
Here we go.

00:06:38.701 --> 00:06:40.033
Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:41.334
That's a goodie.
That's a good one.

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:42.534
"Yeah, you don't trust me?

00:06:44.434 --> 00:06:46.534
Come on. I can do it."

00:06:46.534 --> 00:06:48.334
Alright, next one here.

00:06:56.601 --> 00:06:59.701
♪♪

00:07:07.033 --> 00:07:08.133
Okay.

00:07:08.133 --> 00:07:09.868
Let's see the results
on that one.

00:07:09.868 --> 00:07:14.367
Yeah!
♪♪

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:17.601
You have to, right?
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:17.601 --> 00:07:18.834
You calling it right now?

00:07:18.834 --> 00:07:20.767
-No, I was wrong on that one.
-You were?

00:07:20.767 --> 00:07:22.567
-Yeah.
-Oh, wow. Interesting.

00:07:22.567 --> 00:07:24.033
I would be
a little disappointed.

00:07:24.033 --> 00:07:27.000
He has to do that, right?
Yeah. Next up.

00:07:33.968 --> 00:07:36.567
♪♪

00:07:36.567 --> 00:07:38.133
Oh, don't -- You're playing
the theme wrong.

00:07:38.133 --> 00:07:41.000
You're not even playing
the waiting theme.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:44.400
Yeah. At least give it --

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:45.901
Give it a fighting chance.

00:07:45.901 --> 00:07:48.000
You start playing
depressing music after it,

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.901
what are they supposed to do?

00:07:49.901 --> 00:07:51.834
It's like when "The Brady Bunch"
had a serious --

00:07:51.834 --> 00:07:55.033
♪ Womp, womp, wa-na ♪

00:07:55.033 --> 00:07:58.067
No, it's corn cones, man.

00:07:59.167 --> 00:08:01.934
I'm thumbs-upping it
right now, man. Corn cones.

00:08:01.934 --> 00:08:04.234
I want to see that happen.
Kellogg's, you hearing me?

00:08:04.234 --> 00:08:05.701
Let's see the results.

00:08:05.701 --> 00:08:07.234
Oh, my...
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.234 --> 00:08:09.133
[ Sad tuba plays ]

00:08:09.133 --> 00:08:13.033
Oh, my God.
[ Laughs ]

00:08:13.033 --> 00:08:15.901
Oh, my -- Oh, my gosh.

00:08:15.901 --> 00:08:17.534
I've never seen
that result ever.

00:08:17.534 --> 00:08:19.767
-Yeah.
-And I voted "yes" for you.

00:08:19.767 --> 00:08:21.934
-Our audiences are
on the same page tonight.

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:23.901
-I think I may have
doubled or tripled down on it.

00:08:23.901 --> 00:08:26.234
-No, it doesn't matter.
You can only vote once.

00:08:26.234 --> 00:08:28.300
Alright, the last one here
for "WeTweet."

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:29.334
This last one is...

00:08:33.667 --> 00:08:36.167
♪♪
That's pretty funny.

00:08:36.167 --> 00:08:38.567
"Hey, I'm a hot-tub guy.

00:08:38.567 --> 00:08:40.367
Hey, don't worry about it."

00:08:40.367 --> 00:08:41.868
"What does your husband do?"

00:08:41.868 --> 00:08:45.100
"I'm a hot-tub guy. What's up?
Let's get in there, man.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:46.667
Let's...

00:08:46.667 --> 00:08:50.200
Let's touch kneecaps
and see what's up.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:51.200
Don't worry about it, man.
We all got it, right?

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:52.267
Come on, man.

00:08:52.267 --> 00:08:53.334
Let's have fun
in this hot tub, man.

00:08:53.334 --> 00:08:54.334
Rub-a-dub-dub."

00:08:54.334 --> 00:08:57.467
-Rick. His name's always Rick.

00:08:57.467 --> 00:08:59.601
-His name's always Ricky?
-Right.

00:08:59.601 --> 00:09:01.133
-"Ricky The Hot-Tub Guy."

00:09:01.133 --> 00:09:04.000
Alright, let's see
the results on that jam.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:06.434
Oh, not bad!

00:09:06.434 --> 00:09:07.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:09:07.801 --> 00:09:09.367
Whoa!

00:09:09.367 --> 00:09:11.367
That's the winner right there.

00:09:13.234 --> 00:09:14.300
[ Dinging ]

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.367
That's it!

00:09:16.367 --> 00:09:18.734
I will post this during
commercial break.

00:09:18.734 --> 00:09:20.868
Thank you for helping me out,
helping us out.

00:09:20.868 --> 00:09:22.901
If you see it on your feed,
give it a like,

00:09:22.901 --> 00:09:24.968
give it a "WeTweet," and enjoy.

